WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.862
Myth: a city is hot only because

2
00:00:02.862 --> 00:00:04.174
of the weather.

3
00:00:04.174 --> 00:00:06.276
Fact: the city itself makes some of

4
00:00:06.276 --> 00:00:07.330
that heat.

5
00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:08.821
On the same day,

6
00:00:08.821 --> 00:00:10.691
a city centre is often warmer than

7
00:00:10.691 --> 00:00:12.188
the fields around it.

8
00:00:12.188 --> 00:00:13.953
That warm patch is called an urban

9
00:00:13.953 --> 00:00:15.135
heat island.

10
00:00:15.536 --> 00:00:17.614
Roads and roofs absorb more of the

11
00:00:17.614 --> 00:00:20.737
Sun's heat than trees and soil do,

12
00:00:20.737 --> 00:00:23.199
and give it off after sunset.

13
00:00:23.199 --> 00:00:26.239
Vehicles and air conditioners add even more.

14
00:00:26.638 --> 00:00:28.658
Trees and lakes do the opposite.

15
00:00:28.658 --> 00:00:29.401
They give shade,

16
00:00:29.401 --> 00:00:31.119
and cool the air as water evaporates

17
00:00:31.119 --> 00:00:32.743
from leaves and ponds.

18
00:00:33.143 --> 00:00:34.478
In American studies,

19
00:00:34.478 --> 00:00:36.278
cities ran up to about seven degrees

20
00:00:36.278 --> 00:00:38.333
Fahrenheit warmer by day,

21
00:00:38.333 --> 00:00:40.225
and up to five at night.

22
00:00:40.225 --> 00:00:43.102
Warmer nights give the body less relief.

23
00:00:43.503 --> 00:00:45.453
The fixes are simple to name:

24
00:00:45.453 --> 00:00:49.412
more trees, green roofs or light-coloured roofs,

25
00:00:49.412 --> 00:00:51.433
and pavements that reflect sunlight instead of

26
00:00:51.433 --> 00:00:52.580
storing it.

27
00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:53.932
For GS One,

28
00:00:53.932 --> 00:00:55.743
link this to urbanisation:

29
00:00:55.743 --> 00:00:57.345
how we build a city changes its

30
00:00:57.345 --> 00:00:57.972
climate.

31
00:00:57.972 --> 00:01:00.432
Quote one cause and one fix.

